- introduction

This chapter introduces the topic
  (means) an overview of the subject

Context determines meaning
  (e.g.) the same word has different senses in different domains

- main concepts

The central idea of the subject
  (means) the core principle underlying everything

Supporting concept A relates to the main idea
  (note) worth memorizing separately

Supporting concept B also matters
  (e.g.) practical application of concept B

- advanced topics

Advanced topic builds on main concepts
  (means) deeper understanding requires the foundation

Edge cases are important to understand
  (note) they reveal the limits of the model
